// RHYTHM BANKRUPTCY — HIGHLIFE — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// RHYTHM BANKRUPTCY as West African highlife leaning into afrobeat — a game alternate of
// rhythm, selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces
// the live song. E.T. Mensah, "Sweet Mother", early Fela, the palm-wine guitar.
// 
// THE IDEA: the theme's own ARPEGGIO (rhythm.js's cycle-one lead, the figure the coin fills
// were authored against) was always a highlife guitar ostinato — a fixed figure over a moving
// I–vi–IV–V. GUITAR 1 (FRPP-6 clean electric) plays it verbatim high on the neck; GUITAR 2
// (neck pickup) weaves a counter-line through its holes, so the back half of every bar is a
// hocket; GUITAR 3 is the palm-wine THUMB (alternating root and fifth) in the intro and the
// breakdown; the LEAD GUITAR (bridge pickup) sings the POPCORN hook in sixths; a palm-muted
// CHOP guitar takes every off-beat, strummed down.
// 
// THE HORNS: trumpet (rm7AmBrassLead) leads, a sax (mrdrSaxophone) harmonises in thirds and
// doubles an octave down, a horn section (mrdrHornStab) punches. Call and response twice: in
// the HEAD the trumpet calls the theme's call figure (C . G . G A E) alone and the section
// answers it in thirds with stabs; in the CHORUS trumpet and sax state the Popcorn hook in
// octaves and the section answers in its beat of rest.
// 
// THE BED is rhythm.js's doo-wop turnaround, a chord every half bar — A | C Am | F G |,
// B | C Am | Dm G |, C | F | G |, D | F G | C |, sixteen bars A A B A | A B C D. Under the
// ARP the band voices G without its third (a G5 chop, the bass on G and D): a B under its C
// would be a minor ninth. The shout lifts to D (the original's own lift) through A7sus4 · A7;
// a pivot bar, D · G7, brings the loop home to C.
// 
//   1–4    PALM-WINE — guitar 1 on the ARP over guitar 3's thumb, kick and bell; guitar 2, shekere and clave from bar 3 (the cabinet screen loops 1–4)
//   5–8    THE BAND — bass, chop guitar, congas, cross-stick, hats, shaker; the ARP's climbing tail and a talking-drum call into
//   9–24   HEAD — the trumpet CALLS the theme's call figure, the section ANSWERS in thirds with stabs; 13–16 the guitars alone in front; 21–24 the whole section
//   25–40  CHORUS — the POPCORN HOOK on trumpet and sax in octaves, the horn section answering in its beat of rest; snare and afrobeat hats; talking drum
//   41–48  BREAKDOWN — the guitars interlock alone over the kick and the bell: the ARP and the thumb, guitar 2 from 45, the chop from 47; congas and a roll back in
//   49–56  GUITAR BREAK — the lead guitar sings the hook in sixths, the horn section answers; the lift bar (A7sus4 · A7) with the horns climbing into
//   57–72  SHOUT CHORUS in D — everyone: horns in octaves, the lead guitar in sixths, all four guitars, ghost snares; the pivot D · G7 and the loop goes back to bar 9
// 
// PERCUSSION: agogô bell (cbAgogoWide) on a rolling 4/4 line, son clave, shekere on the
// off-beats, shaker sixteenths, congas in a tumbao, a talking drum at the phrase ends, and a
// light Breakbeat kit — cross-stick in the head, snare on 2 and 4 with afrobeat hats in the
// choruses, ghosts in the shout.
// 
// THE BEAT CABINET'S CLOCK IS KEPT: 124 BPM straight, 4/4, phrases of four bars from bar 1,
// the kick on every quarter of every bar (the breakdown's guitars interlock over the kick and
// the bell), and the loop 9–72 is sixteen whole 16-beat chart loops.
// 
// Levels measured (solo LUFS through the master chain, _remix-bounce --lanes --range) against the
// remix targets (kick ≈ lead, bass 1–3 under, snare 3–6 under, ostinatos 6–9 under, hats 12–16 under):
//   chorus 25–40  trumpet −25.1, kick −24.8, bass −27.1, snare −30.8, sax −32.8, stabs −33.6,
//                 guitar 1 −32.8, guitar 2 −33.3, chop −36.0, hats −37.8, congas −37 to −42
//   head 9–24     trumpet −23.7 against kick −24.1; cross-stick +4 to sit near the chorus snare
//   breakdown     the kick 4 dB down (bar gain, inside the verifier's −6) to −26.8 under guitar 1
//                 −28.5, guitar 2 −31.5, the thumb −32.4
//   guitar break  lead guitar +3 to −24 against kick −24.1; shout: lead guitar 2 dB under the trumpet
// Trailing master gain -4.7 dB for −21.0 LUFS integrated, the whole song (peak −5.1 dBFS).
// 72 bars at 124, 139 s; the loop 9–72 is 124 s.
// Written by work/local/_rhythm-remix-highlife.mjs through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs, which
// self-checks chord tones, passing notes, semitone clashes, one note per string in real
// shapes, strum parity, the loop wrap and the beat cabinet's landmarks; re-running it
// rewrites this file.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
